From: Marius Schneider <marius.schnd@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 14:57:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Derive capability-specific playback tokens from one login

TIDAL grants playback capabilities per client id, not per account: with the
default client id a HI_RES_LOSSLESS request silently degrades to LOSSLESS even
on a MAX subscription. Both tokens are derivable from the refresh token of a
single existing login, so no second login is needed.

Adds ProfileTokenManager (caches per-profile tokens, rotates the refresh token
when the server hands back a new one), parameterises AuthClient with the client
id/secret/refresh style each profile needs, and lets TidalClient send the
matching X-Tidal-Token header.

Verified against a live account: hires -> 24bit/96kHz, default -> 16bit/44.1kHz.

Core subset of PR #427; the CLI-side profile wiring is not used here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
